From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miguel Salinas <mikeys@me.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:09:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(durable): beforeRetry hook decides whether a failed
 attempt is retried

A host often has its own rules for which failed model requests are worth
asking again: an endpoint it knows retries for itself, a transport error it
caused, a refusal that a changed request avoids. settings.retry only offers
pi-ai's fixed classifier and a backoff, so such a host had to turn Pi's retry
off and retry outside the Harness.

GenerationHooks.beforeRetry(failed, api) is asked for every failed attempt that
would retry or end the run: a failed message (model_error) and a request or
poll the host stopped during (interrupted). It gets the attempt, the error and
the policy's own decision (delayMs, absent when the policy would end the run).
The first decision wins: { retry: true, delayMs? } retries, also past
maxRetries or with the policy disabled; { retry: false } ends the run; no
decision leaves it to the policy.
